Subject: Backport upstream PHP 8.x musl fopencookie off_t * seeker signature to PHP 5.6
Policy-Class: P2-Package
Rationale: musl declares cookie_seek_function_t as int (*)(void *, off_t *, int) and does not expose glibc's __off64_t/off64_t unless _LARGEFILE64_SOURCE is set, causing PHP 5.6's configure probe to fall back to the obsolete glibc 2.0 by-value off_t seeker signature (rejected by Clang 20 -Wincompatible-function-pointer-types). Backport PHP 8.x's off_t * fallback signature in main/streams/cast.c.
Upstream-Status: Backport (upstream PHP 8.x musl fopencookie compatibility)
Fil-C-Origin-Commits: none
Origin-Kind: backport
Origin-Project: php/php-src

diff --git a/main/streams/cast.c b/main/streams/cast.c
index 0603a72..a189c39 100644
--- a/main/streams/cast.c
+++ b/main/streams/cast.c
@@ -110,7 +110,10 @@ static ssize_t stream_cookie_writer(void *cookie, const char *buffer, size_t siz
 }
 
 # ifdef COOKIE_SEEKER_USES_OFF64_T
-static int stream_cookie_seeker(void *cookie, __off64_t *position, int whence)
+static int stream_cookie_seeker(void *cookie, off64_t *position, int whence)
+# else
+static int stream_cookie_seeker(void *cookie, off_t *position, int whence)
+# endif
 {
 	TSRMLS_FETCH();
 
@@ -121,14 +124,6 @@ static int stream_cookie_seeker(void *cookie, __off64_t *position, int whence)
 	}
 	return 0;
 }
-# else
-static int stream_cookie_seeker(void *cookie, off_t position, int whence)
-{
-	TSRMLS_FETCH();
-
-	return php_stream_seek((php_stream *)cookie, position, whence);
-}
-# endif
 
 static int stream_cookie_closer(void *cookie)
 {
